        <section>
            <h2>2. The Blind Relay: What I Can’t See, I Can’t Give Away</h2>
            <p><b>The Advantage:</b> Traditional servers log your IP address and connection times. My "Blind Relay" doctrine makes the server a mere conduit.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><span class="highlight">Instant IP Discard:</span> The moment you connect, your IP address is processed in volatile RAM and instantly overwritten. No logs. No history. No trail.</li>
                <li><span class="highlight">RAM-to-RAM Delivery:</span> Messages move from your device's memory to the recipient's memory. Once delivered, they are purged from my relay.</li>
                <li><span class="highlight">Zero Knowledge:</span> Because of my "Scorched Metadata" standard, the server doesn't even know the name or type of the file you sent. To me, everything is just unreadable noise.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>3. Forensic Shredding: Beyond Simple Deletion</h2>
            <p><b>The Advantage:</b> On most phones, "deleted" messages stay on the storage chip, waiting for recovery software to find them.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><span class="highlight">Active Decay:</span> When I delete a message in SecureMessenger, I don't just "hide" it. I trigger a forensic-grade overwrite, replacing your data with random noise before purging it from the silicon.</li>
                <li><span class="highlight">Hardware-Anchored Security:</span> Your encryption keys are "trapped" inside your phone’s Hardware Secure Element (TEE). Even if your phone is lost or stolen, your data remains an unbreakable vault.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>4. The Sovereign Handshake: Invisible by Default</h2>
            <p><b>The Advantage:</b> Stop "Discovery Probing." In other apps, anyone with your number can find you. Here, you are invisible until you choose to be seen.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><span class="highlight">24-Hour Invites:</span> Connect using temporary 6-digit codes that expire.</li>
                <li><span class="highlight">Ghost Mode:</span> Stay invisible even while active. Your "Online" status is your business, not your contacts'.</li>
                <li><span class="highlight">Silent Block:</span> Declining an invite doesn't just block a user—it drops their data at the kernel level. They won't even know they've been ignored.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
